  "name": "blog.rust-lang.org",
  "description": "The official static site repository for the Rust programming language blog, utilizing the Jekyll framework to facilitate technical communication regarding language design and ecosystem milestones. It preserves the historical narrative of Rust’s development, including the transition to 1.0, the introduction of Cargo, and the formalization of its core memory safety and concurrency models. The project integrates Liquid templating and Sass for modular styling and automated syndication through Atom/RSS feeds.",
